January 7

[LINK: (Yoshi's New Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi%27s_New_Island]  is a 2014  [LINK: (platform game) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platformer]  developed by  [LINK: (Arzest) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arzest]  and published by  [LINK: (Nintendo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo]  for the  [LINK: (Nintendo 3DS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_3DS] . The third installment in the  [LINK: (Yoshi's Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi_(video_game_series)]  series, it is set between the events of  [LINK: (Yoshi's Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi%27s_Island]  (1995) and  [LINK: (Yoshi's Island DS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi%27s_Island_DS]  (2006). Like its predecessors, Yoshi's New Island's  [LINK: (gameplay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gameplay]  revolves around safely transporting the infant  [LINK: (Mario) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario]  to his brother  [LINK: (Luigi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luigi_(character)]  by completing a series of  [LINK: (levels) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Level_(video_games)]  across an island. The  [LINK: (player characters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Player_character]  are dinosaurs known as the  [LINK: (Yoshi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi]  species; each dinosaur is named Yoshi and has a unique color. Yoshi's New Island received mixed reviews from critics, who praised its sense of charm and  [LINK: (nostalgia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nostalgia] , but were divided on its art style, level design, and difficulty. Criticism was directed toward its  [LINK: (soundtrack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_game_music] —which some considered repetitive—and the game's perceived lack of originality in comparison to its predecessors. The game was reissued as part of the  [LINK: (Nintendo Selects) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_Selects]  line in 2016, and by 2020, it had sold more than two million copies worldwide. Yoshi's New Island was succeeded by  [LINK: (Yoshi's Woolly World) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi%27s_Woolly_World]  for the  [LINK: (Wii U) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_U]  in 2015. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi%27s_New_Island] )

