January 9

[LINK: (Political philosophy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_philosophy]  studies the theoretical and conceptual foundations of  [LINK: (politics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politics] . It examines the nature, scope, and  [LINK: (legitimacy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_legitimacy]  of political institutions, such as  [LINK: (states) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_(polity)] . It investigates different  [LINK: (forms of government) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government#Forms] , ranging from  [LINK: (democracy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democracy]  to  [LINK: (authoritarianism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authoritarianism] , and the values guiding political action, like  [LINK: (justice) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice] , equality, and  [LINK: (liberty) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberty] . Political philosophy focuses on desirable norms and values, in contrast to  [LINK: (political science) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_science] , which emphasizes  [LINK: (empirical) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empirical_evidence]  description. Political philosophy has its roots in  [LINK: (antiquity) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_history] , such as the theories of  [LINK: (Plato) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plato]  and  [LINK: (Aristotle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aristotle]  (both pictured) in  [LINK: (ancient Greek philosophy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek_philosophy] , with discussions on the nature of justice and ideal states.  [LINK: (Confucianism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confucianism] ,  [LINK: (Taoism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taoism] , and  [LINK: (legalism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legalism_(Chinese_philosophy)]  emerged in  [LINK: (ancient Chinese philosophy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_philosophy#Ancient_philosophy] , while  [LINK: (Hindu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hinduism]  and  [LINK: (Buddhist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddhism]  political thought developed in  [LINK: (ancient India) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_ancient_India] . The modern period marked a shift towards  [LINK: (secularism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secularism]  as diverse schools of thought developed, such as  [LINK: (social contract theory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_contract] , liberalism, conservatism,  [LINK: (utilitarianism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utilitarianism] ,  [LINK: (Marxism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marxism] , and anarchism. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_philosophy] )

