January 10

The  [LINK: (2021 Masters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Masters_(snooker)]  (officially the 2021 Betfred Masters) was a professional non-ranking  [LINK: (snooker) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snooker]  tournament that took place from 10 to 17 January 2021 at the  [LINK: (Marshall Arena) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arena_MK]  in  [LINK: (Milton Keynes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milton_Keynes] , England. It was the 47th staging of the  [LINK: (Masters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masters_(snooker)] , which was  [LINK: (first held in 1975) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1975_Masters_(snooker)] , and the second of three  [LINK: (Triple Crown) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triple_Crown_(snooker)]  events in the  [LINK: (2020–21 season) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020%E2%80%9321_snooker_season] . The top sixteen players from the  [LINK: (snooker world rankings) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snooker_world_rankings]  were invited to compete in a  [LINK: (knockout tournament) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single-elimination_tournament] , organised by the  [LINK: (World Professional Billiards and Snooker Association) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Professional_Billiards_and_Snooker_Association] . It was played  [LINK: (behind closed doors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Behind_closed_doors_(sport)]  because of  [LINK: (COVID-19 restrictions in the United Kingdom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic_in_the_United_Kingdom] . The defending champion,  [LINK: (Stuart Bingham) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_Bingham] , had defeated  [LINK: (Ali Carter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Carter]  10–8 in the  [LINK: (2020 Masters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Masters_(snooker)]  final. Bingham lost 6–5 to  [LINK: (Yan Bingtao) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yan_Bingtao]  (pictured) in the semi-finals. Yan (one of three debutants at the event, alongside  [LINK: (Thepchaiya Un-Nooh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thepchaiya_Un-Nooh]  and  [LINK: (Gary Wilson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gary_Wilson_(snooker_player)] ) met  [LINK: (John Higgins) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Higgins]  in the final. Yan completed a 10–8 victory to win his first Triple Crown tournament. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Masters_(snooker)] )

