January 13

" [LINK: (Shine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shine_(Gwen_Stefani_song)] " is a song written and recorded by American singer  [LINK: (Gwen Stefani) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gwen_Stefani]  (pictured) featuring  [LINK: (Pharrell Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharrell_Williams] , who also produced the song. Originally intended for Stefani's band  [LINK: (No Doubt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Doubt] , it is a  [LINK: (reggae pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reggae_fusion]  and  [LINK: (ska) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ska]  song that was written for the 2014 live-action/animated film  [LINK: (Paddington) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddington_(film)] . The lyrics revolve around the lead character  [LINK: (Paddington Bear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddington_Bear] 's journey to London and his identity crisis. Stefani initially disagreed with Williams' choice to use direct references to Paddington in the lyrics, but praised this decision after watching the film with her children. She reported that her involvement with the recording was inspired by her then-husband  [LINK: (Gavin Rossdale) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gavin_Rossdale]  and her children's connection to England. Critical response to "Shine" was mixed; some praised Stefani and Williams's chemistry, while others compared it negatively to their previous collaborations. Commentators frequently likened it to Williams's 2013 single " [LINK: (Happy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happy_(Pharrell_Williams_song)] " and Stefani's 2014 song " [LINK: (Spark the Fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spark_the_Fire] ". ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shine_(Gwen_Stefani_song)] )

