January 16

[LINK: (Batman Returns) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_Returns]  is a 1992 American  [LINK: (superhero film) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superhero_film]  directed by  [LINK: (Tim Burton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Burton]  and written by  [LINK: (Daniel Waters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Waters_(screenwriter)] . Based on the  [LINK: (DC Comics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DC_Comics]  character  [LINK: (Batman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman] , it is the sequel to  [LINK: (Batman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_(1989_film)]  (1989) and the second installment in the  [LINK: (Batman film series) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_in_film#Tim_Burton_and_Joel_Schumacher_series]  (1989–1997). Set during Christmas in  [LINK: (Gotham City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham_City] , the film follows  [LINK: (Batman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Wayne_(1989_film_series_character)] , played by  [LINK: (Michael Keaton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Keaton]  (pictured), as he confronts corrupt businessman Max Shreck ( [LINK: (Christopher Walken) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christopher_Walken] ) and deformed crime boss  [LINK: (Oswald Cobblepot / the Penguin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penguin_in_other_media#Film]  ( [LINK: (Danny DeVito) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danny_DeVito] ), whose bid for power threatens the city. Their schemes are further complicated by Shreck's former secretary  [LINK: (Selina Kyle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selina_Kyle_(Batman_Returns)]  ( [LINK: (Michelle Pfeiffer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michelle_Pfeiffer] ), who seeks revenge against him as Catwoman. Released in June 1992, Batman Returns broke several box-office records and grossed $266.8 million worldwide, becoming the sixth-highest-grossing  [LINK: (film of 1992) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_in_film] . Critical reception was polarized, though most reviewers praised the principal cast. Following the film's mixed reception, Burton was replaced as director for its sequel,  [LINK: (Batman Forever) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_Forever]  (1995). ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_Returns] )

