January 18

The  [LINK: (2017 Africa Cup of Nations final) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Africa_Cup_of_Nations_final]  was an  [LINK: (association football) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_football]  match to determine the winner of the  [LINK: (2017 Africa Cup of Nations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Africa_Cup_of_Nations] , organised by the  [LINK: (Confederation of African Football) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confederation_of_African_Football]  (CAF). It was held at the  [LINK: (Stade de l'Amitié) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stade_d%27Angondj%C3%A9]  in  [LINK: (Libreville) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libreville] , Gabon, and contested by  [LINK: (Cameroon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameroon_national_football_team]  (team pictured) and  [LINK: (Egypt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt_national_football_team] . Egypt took a 1–0 lead through  [LINK: (Mohamed Elneny) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohamed_Elneny]  after 22 minutes. Cameroon had more possession than Egypt in the first half, but their attack lacked potency and Egypt led at half time. The Egyptians made few attempts to attack in the second half, and Cameroon equalised after 59 minutes through  [LINK: (Nicolas Nkoulou) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Nkoulou] , who had come on as a  [LINK: (substitute) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Substitute_(association_football)] . Egypt were unable to adjust, and Cameroon continued to have the better chances, eventually scoring again two minutes before the end, through  [LINK: (Vincent Aboubakar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincent_Aboubakar] , to record a 2–1 win. The victory marked their fifth  [LINK: (Africa Cup of Nations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Africa_Cup_of_Nations]  title. As winners, they represented CAF at the  [LINK: (2017 FIFA Confederations Cup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_FIFA_Confederations_Cup]  in Russia, but they did not progress beyond the group phase. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Africa_Cup_of_Nations_final] )

