January 22

[LINK: (The First Vision) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_First_Vision]  is the debut video album by  [LINK: (Mariah Carey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariah_Carey]  (pictured), released on January 22, 1991. It is a collection of music videos, live performances, and film footage detailing the development and promotion of Carey's first studio album  [LINK: (Mariah Carey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariah_Carey_(album)] . It features music videos of " [LINK: (Vision of Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vision_of_Love] ", " [LINK: (Love Takes Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Takes_Time] ", and " [LINK: (Someday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Someday_(Mariah_Carey_song)] ", as well as snippets of future singles " [LINK: (I Don't Wanna Cry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Don%27t_Wanna_Cry] " and " [LINK: (There's Got to Be a Way) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/There%27s_Got_to_Be_a_Way] ". The collection presents Carey performing at Club Tatou and rehearsal footage for  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live]  and  [LINK: (It's Showtime at the Apollo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Showtime_at_the_Apollo] . During an interview segment, Carey answers questions about her life and music. Critics considered the album insightful and praised the showcase of her live vocal abilities; others opined that it projected her in a sexual manner. The video peaked at numbers 2 and 24 respectively on US and UK music video charts. The  [LINK: (Canadian Recording Industry Association) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_Canada]  certified it gold and the  [LINK: (Recording Industry Association of America) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recording_Industry_Association_of_America]  certified it platinum. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_First_Vision] )

