January 25

[LINK: (CSS General Earl Van Dorn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS_General_Earl_Van_Dorn]  was a  [LINK: (cottonclad warship) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottonclad_warship]  used by the  [LINK: (Confederate States of America) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confederate_States_of_America]  during the  [LINK: (American Civil War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War] . Purchased for Confederate service in  [LINK: (New Orleans) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Orleans]  in early 1862 to serve with the  [LINK: (River Defense Fleet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Defense_Fleet] , she was converted into a cottonclad warship by installing an iron-covered framework of timbers on her  [LINK: (bow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bow_(watercraft)]  that served as a  [LINK: (ram) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naval_ram] , and protecting her machinery with timber bulkheads packed with cotton. A  [LINK: (sidewheel steamer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddle_steamer] , she was 182 feet (55 m) long and was armed with a single  [LINK: (32-pounder cannon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/32-pounder_gun]  on the bow. Initially assigned to defend the  [LINK: (Mississippi River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mississippi_River] , she arrived at  [LINK: (Memphis, Tennessee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis,_Tennessee] , in April 1862. On May 10, she fought with the River Defense Fleet against the  [LINK: (Union navy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_navy]  in the  [LINK: (Battle of Plum Point Bend) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Plum_Point_Bend]  (pictured), where she rammed and sank  [LINK: (USS Mound City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Mound_City] . After withdrawing up the  [LINK: (Yazoo River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yazoo_River]  to  [LINK: (Liverpool Landing, Mississippi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liverpool,_Mississippi] , General Earl Van Dorn, along with two other warships, was burnt to prevent her capture by approaching Union vessels. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS_General_Earl_Van_Dorn] )

