January 26

[LINK: (Louis Leblanc) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Leblanc]  (born January 26, 1991) is a former professional  [LINK: (ice hockey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_hockey]  player. A  [LINK: (centre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_(ice_hockey)] , Leblanc played  [LINK: (minor hockey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minor_ice_hockey]  in the  [LINK: (Montreal region) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Montreal]  before playing one season with the  [LINK: (Omaha Lancers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omaha_Lancers]  and becoming Rookie of the Year. At the  [LINK: (2009 NHL entry draft) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_NHL_entry_draft] , he was selected 18th overall by the  [LINK: (Montreal Canadiens) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montreal_Canadiens] . He then spent one season with  [LINK: (Harvard Crimson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvard_Crimson_men%27s_ice_hockey] , being named  [LINK: (Ivy League) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivy_League]  rookie of the year, before signing a contract with the Canadiens in 2010. Later that year, Leblanc joined the  [LINK: (Montreal Juniors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montreal_Junior_Hockey_Club] . He spent three seasons with the Canadiens, mainly playing for their  [LINK: (American Hockey League) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Hockey_League]  affiliate, before being traded in 2014 to the  [LINK: (Anaheim Ducks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anaheim_Ducks] , who kept him in the AHL. In 2015, Leblanc moved to Europe, joining  [LINK: (HC Slovan Bratislava) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HC_Slovan_Bratislava] , playing seven games before being released. He appeared in four games for  [LINK: (Lausanne HC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lausanne_HC] , then retired from hockey. Internationally, Leblanc played in the  [LINK: (2008 Ivan Hlinka Memorial Tournament) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Ivan_Hlinka_Memorial_Tournament]  and the  [LINK: (2011 World Junior Ice Hockey Championships) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2011_World_Junior_Ice_Hockey_Championships] . ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Leblanc] )

