January 27

[LINK: (Thousands of Jews lived in the towns of Dęblin and Irena) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_the_Jews_in_D%C4%99blin_and_Irena_during_World_War_II]  in central Poland before World War II. In September 1939, the towns were captured in the  [LINK: (German invasion of Poland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invasion_of_Poland]  and the persecution of Jews began with drafts into  [LINK: (forced labor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forced_labour]  and the start of a  [LINK: (Judenrat) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judenrat] . An  [LINK: (open ghetto) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_ghettos_established_by_Nazi_Germany]  was made in Irena and its inhabitants worked on labor projects for  [LINK: (Dęblin Fortress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C4%99blin_Fortress] , the railway, and the  [LINK: (Luftwaffe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luftwaffe] . Beginning in May 1941, Jews were sent to labor camps around  [LINK: (Dęblin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C4%99blin]  from the  [LINK: (Opole) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opole#After_World_War_I]  and  [LINK: (Warsaw ghettos) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warsaw_Ghetto] . Conditions in the ghetto worsened due to epidemics of  [LINK: (typhus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typhus]  and  [LINK: (dysentery) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dysentery] . The first deportation was on 6 May 1942 and took around 2,500 Jews to the  [LINK: (Sobibór extermination camp) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sobibor_extermination_camp] . A week later, two thousand Jews  [LINK: (arrived from Slovakia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Holocaust_transports_from_Slovakia]  and hundreds more from nearby ghettos. In October, the Irena ghetto was liquidated; about 2,500 Jews were deported to the  [LINK: (Treblinka extermination camp) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treblinka_extermination_camp]  while some 1,400 Jews were retained as inmates of forced-labor camps. On 27 July 1944, the camp was liberated by the  [LINK: (Red Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Army] . ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_the_Jews_in_D%C4%99blin_and_Irena_during_World_War_II] )

