January 30

" [LINK: (Life on Mars?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F] " is a song by the English musician  [LINK: (David Bowie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Bowie]  (pictured), first released on his 1971 album  [LINK: (Hunky Dory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunky_Dory] . Conceived as a parody of  [LINK: (Frank Sinatra) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Sinatra] 's " [LINK: (My Way) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Way] ", "Life on Mars?" was recorded in August 1971 at  [LINK: (Trident Studios) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trident_Studios]  in London, and was co-produced by Bowie and  [LINK: (Ken Scott) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Scott] . The track features piano by the keyboardist  [LINK: (Rick Wakeman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Wakeman]  and a string arrangement by the guitarist  [LINK: (Mick Ronson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mick_Ronson] . "Life on Mars?" is primarily a  [LINK: (glam rock) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glam_rock]  ballad, with elements of  [LINK: (cabaret) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabaret]  and  [LINK: (art rock) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Art_rock] . The lyrics are about a girl who goes to a cinema to escape reality, and include  [LINK: (surreal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surrealism]  images that reflect optimism and the effects of  [LINK: (Hollywood) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinema_of_the_United_States] . In June 1973, at the height of Bowie's fame as  [LINK: (Ziggy Stardust) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziggy_Stardust_(character)] ,  [LINK: (RCA Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RCA_Records]  issued "Life on Mars?" as a  [LINK: (single) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_(music)]  in the United Kingdom, where it peaked at number three. Bowie frequently performed "Life on Mars?" during his concerts, and the track has appeared on numerous  [LINK: (compilation albums) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compilation_album] . Commentators generally consider "Life on Mars?" to be one of Bowie's finest songs. ( [LINK: (Full article...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_on_Mars%3F] )

